From 745f6b282385cf1a9857bb42238fa5fb6bf8f697 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 13:01:32 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] MUMPS and AmgX: approximate factorization tested, aggregation
 option checked

The block low-rank factorization of MUMPS preconditions the conjugate
gradient of MFEM on a 24^3 cube, where MUMPS compresses fronts: ten
iterations instead of one with the exact factorization (on the 12^3
cube, MUMPS compresses no front, and the approximate factorization was
exact). The matrix is declared symmetric positive definite, the
factorization being then symmetric, as the conjugate gradient assumes.

The conjugate gradient of MFEM preconditioned by AmgX with the option
Multigrid set to Aggregation needs the iterations of the same
configuration given as a string: an ignored option is detected.

Docs: the smoother of the aggregation multigrid is a damped Jacobi
smoother (the block Jacobi smoother of AmgX on blocks of size one), its
V-cycle has no pre-smoothing sweep and is not symmetric; the matrix
given to the MUMPS preconditioner of the conjugate gradient shall be
declared symmetric positive definite.
